course: dictionary
lesson: 5627
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word lime can be a fruit, a colour, a white powder or a tree. The words around it tell you which one. «Acid such as lemon or lime juice unfolds proteins» is about food, because you squeeze juice from a fruit.
explain: «Park a car under a lime tree in July» tells you that lime means a tree here, because you park under it. Ask yourself: what does the sentence say about the lime? Then try each meaning in the sentence and see which one fits.
explain: Lime can also be a colour, as in «lime green», and it can be a powder. «In class, a teacher can have you breathe out gently through a straw into clear lime water» is about a science test, so lime here means the white powder that is mixed into the water, not a fruit.
explain: In «lime green», the word lime describes the colour, so it works like an adjective. The clues in each sentence always decide which meaning is right.
fact: Lime can mean a small round green fruit with sour juice.
fact: Lime can also mean a bright yellow-green colour, as in «lime green».
fact: Lime can mean a white powder made from limestone, used in building and farming.
fact: A lime tree, also called a linden, is a tall tree with heart-shaped leaves.
fact: «Limewater» turns cloudy, or milky, when carbon dioxide is bubbled through it.
exercise: «Park a car under a lime tree in July.» In this sentence, what is a lime? | *A tree | A bright yellow-green colour | A white powder | A small green fruit
exercise: Mia says «lime green» is a colour, not a fruit. Which meaning of lime is used in «lime green»? | A tall tree | *A bright yellow-green colour | A small round green fruit | A white powder for building
exercise: «Breathe out gently through a straw into clear lime water, and it goes milky.» What does the milky change show? | The water is sweet | *Carbon dioxide is in your breath | The lime is ripe | The straw is dirty
test: «Acid such as lemon or lime juice unfolds proteins; fish soaked in lime juice turns white.» Which meaning of lime is used here? | A lime tree | *A small round green citrus fruit with sour juice | A bright yellow-green colour | A white powder used in cement
test: «Limewater turns milky when carbon dioxide is bubbled through it.» What is limewater made from? | Chilli and grasshoppers | *Lime, the white powder, stirred into water | Sweet honeydew | Lime juice and sugar
exam: «Chapulines are toasted grasshoppers with lime and chilli, eaten in Oaxaca in Mexico.» What does lime mean here? | A white powder for building | *A small green fruit with sour juice | A tree | A colour
